      "id": "pf_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": -756,
        "y": 0
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Particle fountain\n\nA Particles patch is four nodes at minimum: time/seconds → Emitter, an Emitter to spawn from, a World to integrate against, and a Render-As to draw the live buffer. Gravity lives on the World and applies to every Emitter wired to it.\n\nDrag tames terminal velocity; the wrap-bounds keep the canvas cycling.",
        "width": 500,
        "height": 260
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Particle fountain\n\nA Particles patch is four nodes at minimum: time/seconds → Emitter, an Emitter to spawn from, a World to integrate against, and a Render-As to draw the live buffer. Gravity lives on the World and applies to every Emitter wired to it.\n\nDrag tames terminal velocity; the wrap-bounds keep the canvas cycling.",
        "width": 500,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
